Module goingbank "The Going Bank" {
  Description "The Gape: a gorge four hundred paces across, a grass-rope bridge, a village on each lip, and an east bank that is not standing still.".

  Place country "the Gape country" is region within imbar.
  Place lip "Tarrow Lip" is settlement within country at 0, 0.
  Place span "the Plait" is site within country at 1, 0.
  Place ketter "Ketter" is settlement within country at 2, 0.
  Place wall "the west wall of the Gape" is site within country at 1, 1.
  Place loft_bld "the plaiters' loft" is building within lip.
  Place inn "the Long Pull" is building within lip.

  Place road "the road up to Tarrow Lip" is room within lip at 0, 0 outdoors.
  Place lip_end "the windlass and toll-board" is room within lip at 1, 0 outdoors.
  Place kite_barn "Halloway's barn" is room within lip at 1, 1 outdoors.
  Place loft "the plaiters' loft" is room within loft_bld at 0, 0.
  Place taproom "the Long Pull's taproom" is room within inn at 0, 0.
  Place seam "the ledge above the Grudge" is room within wall at 0, 0.
  Place plait_west "the west stub of the Plait" is room within span at 0, 0 outdoors.
  Place join "the Join" is room within span at 1, 0 outdoors.
  Place plait_east "the east stub of the Plait" is room within span at 2, 0 outdoors.
  Place landing "Ketter landing" is room within ketter at 0, 0 outdoors.
  Place green "Ketter green" is room within ketter at 1, 0 outdoors.
  Place drum_ridge "the drum-stone" is room within ketter at 1, 1 outdoors.
  Place churchyard "the leaning church" is room within ketter at 2, 0 outdoors.

  Passage lip_road "the last of the road" is road between road and lip_end taking 10 minutes.
  Passage loft_door "the loft door" is door between lip_end and loft.
  Passage inn_door "the Long Pull's door" is door between lip_end and taproom.
  Passage barn_path "the path to the barn" is path between lip_end and kite_barn taking 3 minutes.
  Passage wall_ladder "the ladder down the wall" is ladder between lip_end and seam taking 5 minutes.
  Passage toll_gate "the toll-gate" is gate between lip_end and plait_west.
  Passage span_west "the planks to the Join" is bridge between plait_west and join taking 5 minutes.
  Passage span_east "the span beyond the Join" is bridge between join and plait_east taking 5 minutes.
  Passage east_gate "Ketter's post" is gate between plait_east and landing.
  Passage green_path "the lane to the green" is path between landing and green taking 3 minutes.
  Passage ridge_path "the path up to the drum-stone" is path between green and drum_ridge taking 10 minutes.
  Passage church_path "the churchyard path" is path between green and churchyard taking 3 minutes.

  Observe road_scene at road when true "The road comes up through gorse to a windlass on the lip of the sky. The far side of the Gape is a long green hill with a village on it, and between you and the hill there is only wind.".
  Observe lip_scene at lip_end when true "A windlass, a toll-board, and a bridge of woven grass that goes out over the Gape and stops. Pipit sits on the toll-board with her feet on the Plait. Down the road's last bend the loft smells of green rope.".
  Observe lip_gap at lip_end when not dark() "Across the Gape the Plait comes in from the east and stops too. Between the two ends the gap is the width of a house. The Grudge is a brown thread at the bottom.".
  Observe barn_scene at kite_barn when true "A barn with its roof taken off. In the rafters hangs a kite of sailcloth and bean-poles as wide as a cart, with a harness under it. A hay-scale stands in the doorway, and the wall beside it is chalked with names and weights.".
  Observe loft_scene at loft when true "A long room that smells of green grass and goat. Knot-boards cover the walls, one for each spring's Knotting, and each knot is different. The newest board has a gap in it the width of a hand.".
  Observe taproom_scene at taproom when true "A low room with a settle and a crate of iron pins by the fire. A wedding supper is being argued over at the long table.".
  Observe seam_scene at seam when true "A ledge in the west wall, and the brown Grudge below. Across the river the east wall is not rock. It is grey-brown and ribbed, and lichen grows on it in rounds, as it does on a hide.".
  Observe plait_west_scene at plait_west when true "The Plait ends here in frayed grass, swaying. A line of lashed poles runs on out over the Gape, and a guide-rope on posts beside it.".
  Observe join_scene at join when true "The middle of the Gape, on poles lashed end to end. The wind plays the rope like a string. Both villages are small from here, and neither seems to be moving.".
  Observe plait_east_scene at plait_east when true "The east stub of the Plait, frayed to the same grass. Behind you the lashed walk dwindles over the drop to the Lip.".
  Observe landing_scene at landing when true "A post, a water trough, and a lane up to the green. The trough is full on its east side only.".
  Observe green_scene at green when true "A village green at a slight angle. The sundial gives the wrong hour. A cheese, put down by a cheesewife to cool, rolls gently to the east, and she goes after it without remark.".
  Observe ridge_scene at drum_ridge when true "A bare knoll above Ketter, and on it one hollow grey stone the size of a bed, with a bone drumstick lying across it. Past the knoll the ground ends in sky, a long way east.".
  Observe church_scene at churchyard when true "A little church leaning politely toward the sea. Its bell hangs a half-tone flat. Its graves lean the same way, in rows, like a congregation.".

  Thing cairns "the line of cairns" at green {
    Tries looking.
    State standing "A line of old cairns crosses the green, one to a generation. The oldest stands at the cliff's edge. The newest is by the well.".
  }
  Observe cairns_looked near cairns when tried(cairns, looking) "Each cairn was set on the line from the church door to the first bridge-post. Each is now a little east of it, and the oldest is a hundred paces east, on the brink of the Gape. The line was not moved. The ground under it was." teaches cairns_known.
  Discovery cairns_known "The cairns that were set on one line from church to bridge are each a little further east, the oldest a hundred paces. The ground is going east, not the cairns.".

  Thing hide "the east wall" at seam {
    Tries looking.
    State grey "The east wall of the Gape is ribbed grey-brown, and wet at the foot.".
    Wonder natural unique for aesthetic, scientific, dangerous "Held to a lamp, the east wall is a hide. It rises, slowly, the height of a house, and falls, and a drop of warm water comes off the overhang. It is breathing.".
  }
  Observe hide_looked near hide when tried(hide, looking) "You hold the lamp up to the east wall. The ribs rise, slowly, the height of a house, and fall. Warm water drips from the overhang. The wall shifts one thumb's width, left to right, in the time it takes to say a prayer." teaches walker_known.
  Discovery walker_known "The east bank is the back of a living thing. It breathes, and it is going somewhere.".
  Discovery bank_going "The east bank is going east, a little further every year. The Plait comes out short because the ground is leaving it.".
  Discovery cord_known "Sabra Yarrow has kept a knotted cord forty years: one knot for each pace the Plait came out long on the west side. The knots run ten, twelve, fifty.".
  Discovery drum_known "Meggan Lorrimer's drum-stone answers: the bank, struck, answers back, and the answer says how it feels.".
  Discovery sea_known "The thing under Ketter is going to the sea, as it has before, every ninety years or so.".
  Discovery handline_known "A hand-line laid along the guide-rope would let anybody cross the gap, and Sabra Yarrow sells rope.".
  Discovery wedding_known "Tamsy Hendry and Fell Anstey are to be married on the Join at dusk on the third day, with both villages on the Plait.".
  Discovery kite_known "Bettony's kite flies east on the west wind at dusk, from five till eight. It lifts one at a time, and never the old.".
  Discovery bettony_lost "Bettony Halloway built her kite after her husband went into the Grudge, where no rope was long enough to reach him.".
  Discovery pins_known "Varnish crosses to the Ketter shelf at noon on the second day, and drives his nine pins at the hour of the wedding.".
  Discovery varnish_son "Magne Varnish has a boy of six at the Lip.".
  Discovery fell_afraid "Fell Anstey is afraid of the Join: of saying his vows in the middle of nothing.".
  Discovery wet_said "Osbel Hendry blames the wet for Ketter's flat bell. The well rope is longer every spring, and the big terrace runs downhill the wrong way.".
  Discovery osbel_asks "Osbel Hendry will not hear that the ground is going east until he is told what it is going to.".
  Discovery meggan_present "Meggan Lorrimer has not seen the sea, and means to be present when the hill comes to it.".
  Discovery ketter_choice "Ketter will leave its hill or keep it, as the company tells Osbel Hendry.".
  Discovery boards_seen "In the loft the newest knot-board has a gap in it, and the boards before it show each spring's gap a little wider.".
}
